+|---|---|---|---|
+| `idempotency_key` | string (UUID) | Yes | Client-generated key identifying a logical submission attempt |
+| `visit_id` | string (UUID) | Yes | Client-generated visit identifier |
+| `base_revision_id` | string (UUID) \| null | Yes | Revision the worker edited from, or `null` when creating a new visit |
+| `payload` | VisitPayload | Yes | Complete visit fields: `plot_id`, `observed_at`, `observers`, `species_cover`, `notes` |
 
-## Downstream Contract Work
+Server-assigned metadata stored with every accepted submission:
 
-After selection, define the submission envelope, current-state response, unresolved-work representation, and resolution operation here. Tablet-sync will size its local storage and retry state machine around that envelope. Review-export will size its coordinator interface and export eligibility rules around the unresolved-work representation. Both must link back to this node rather than invent their own concurrency semantics.
+- `revision_id` (UUID)
+- `kind`: `submission`
+- `author_id` (authenticated worker identity)
+- `received_at` (server UTC timestamp)
+
+### Validation and Idempotency
+
+Before persisting a submission, the record store authenticates the submitting worker, validates payload field types and required structure, and verifies that `payload.plot_id` resolves to a known plot in `site-catalog` and that a non-null `base_revision_id` belongs to `visit_id`.
+
+Idempotency is scoped to the authenticated submission envelope:
+
+- Repeating an accepted `idempotency_key` with an identical `visit_id`, `base_revision_id`, and `payload` returns the original acceptance response without creating a new revision.
+- Repeating an accepted `idempotency_key` with any differing `visit_id`, `base_revision_id`, or `payload` is rejected and leaves stored state unchanged.
+
+### Acceptance Response
+
+| Field | Type | Description |
+|---|---|---|
+| `revision_id` | string (UUID) | Assigned ID of the stored revision |
+| `visit_id` | string (UUID) | Visit identifier |
+| `status` | `current` \| `needs_review` | Resulting visit state after accepting this submission |
+| `active_head_ids` | string[] | All active head revision IDs for the visit |
+| `received_at` | timestamp (UTC) | Server receipt time |
+
+## Retrieval and Unresolved Work
+
+The record store exposes three read views to support field sync, coordinator review, and export:
+
+- **Current-state retrieval** (by `visit_id`, or filtered list for export): Returns `visit_id`, `status` (`current` | `needs_review`), `current_revision` (the sole active head when `status` is `current`; `null` when `needs_review`), and `competing_revisions` (empty when `current`; all active head revisions when `needs_review`). Export queries filter strictly to visits with `status: current`.
+- **Review-queue retrieval**: Lists visits currently in `needs_review` state along with their active head summaries (revision IDs, authors, receipt times, and base revision IDs) so coordinators can prioritize and open comparison views.
+- **Revision-history retrieval** (by `visit_id`): Returns the full immutable list of revisions for the visit—both `submission` and `resolution` records—with parent links, authors/coordinators, receipt/resolution times, and complete payloads. This supports side-by-side comparison against common ancestors and end-to-end provenance tracing.
+
+## Conflict Resolution
+
+### Resolution Request
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Description |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `visit_id` | string (UUID) | Yes | Visit being resolved |
+| `expected_head_ids` | string[] | Yes | Exact set of active head revision IDs the coordinator reviewed |
+| `payload` | VisitPayload | Yes | Complete resolved visit payload (either matching one competing revision or coordinator-edited) |
+| `resolution_note` | string | No | Optional coordinator explanation stored with the resolution |
+
+Server-assigned metadata stored with every resolution:
+
+- `revision_id` (UUID)
+- `kind`: `resolution`
+- `coordinator_id` (authenticated coordinator identity)
+- `parent_revision_ids` (the superseded `expected_head_ids`)
+- `resolved_at` (server UTC timestamp)
+
+### Optimistic Concurrency on Resolution
+
+A resolution succeeds only if `expected_head_ids` matches the visit's exact set of active heads at commit time and the visit is in `needs_review`. If another competing submission arrived while the coordinator was reviewing, the server rejects the resolution with a conflict error returning the updated active head set so no unseen submission is silently superseded.
+
+Original submissions remain intact in the revision history after resolution; the resolution revision records the contributing head IDs and coordinator identity without mutating prior revisions.
+
+## Downstream Contract Obligations
+
+- **`tablet-sync`**: Retains `base_revision_id` for each locally cached visit and includes it in whole-visit submissions alongside a persistent `idempotency_key`. Uses the acceptance response's `status` to inform field workers when their edit created or joined a competing revision awaiting coordinator review.
+- **`review-export`**: Uses review-queue and revision-history retrieval to present whole-visit side-by-side comparisons, submits resolutions with `expected_head_ids`, and excludes visits with `status: needs_review` from the Friday partner CSV export.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Concurrent visit edit policy | Whole-visit revisions with coordinator review | Field-aware three-way merge | Preserves each submitted visit as a scientifically coherent unit and prevents automated merge rules from silently combining scientifically related edits (such as species identification and cover estimate). Avoids building and maintaining field-level merge rules, aligning with operation by two coordinators without a dedicated systems administrator, at the cost of routing disjoint concurrent edits to the review queue. See [Concurrent Visit Edit Policy](decisions/concurrent-visit-edits.md). |
+| Resolution concurrency guard | Require `expected_head_ids` matching all active heads | Resolve unconditionally against current heads | Prevents a coordinator from inadvertently superseding a newly arrived competing revision they never saw on the comparison screen. |
+| Resolution storage representation | Immutable `resolution` revision in the same DAG | Mutable "resolved" pointer or overwriting a winning revision | Keeps provenance uniform across submissions and resolutions, preserves all original submissions untouched, and naturally handles late offline edits arriving after a prior resolution. |
